# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines who is expected to review changes to each part of the
# repository. It exists from day one, even with a single maintainer,
# because "who has final say on this PR" should never be ambiguous —
# see CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# As subsystem ownership is handed off to trusted contributors (see
# CONTRIBUTING.md), add their GitHub usernames to the relevant lines
# below rather than leaving everything owned by the core maintainer(s).

# Default owner for anything not covered by a more specific rule below.
*                           @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers

# Architecture Decision Records require core maintainer review —
# these are the project's load-bearing decisions (see ADR-0000/0001).
/docs/adr/                  @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers

# Runtime core packages
/internal/server/           @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/internal/pipeline/         @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/internal/storage/          @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/internal/cache/            @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/internal/cli/              @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/internal/config/           @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/cmd/                       @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/deploy/                    @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers

# Governance-adjacent files always require core maintainer sign-off.
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/CODEOWNERS                 @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
/LICENSE                    @OPTIVOR_ORG/core-maintainers
